    {
      "blockId": "tour:itinerary_text:b04d5d61d358e759",
      "field": "itinerary.text",
      "sourceTextSha256": "ccaec431fa65b7dcfd9f6a96d028288a8cfe0ffe67ca7f6b14fb7c591a2c4d85",
      "text": "Day 5 · A visit to Tikal, 64 km from Flores, the most important Maya site in Guatemala and one of the largest cities of the Maya world. Inhabited from around the 6th century BC to the 10th century AD, it was then reclaimed by the jungle until its rediscovery and restoration. Its urban core covered some 16 km², with about 3,000 structures, and its six great temple-pyramids rise above the forest like skyscrapers, earning Tikal the nickname “New York of the Maya”. Tikal National Park covers 575 km² and has been a UNESCO World Heritage Site, for both its cultural and natural value, since 1979. Flight back to Guatemala City. Overnight at Hotel Barceló Guatemala City. (B)",
      "provenance": {
        "kind": "word_exact",
